framework ArchitectureDecisionRecord:
  requires problem and decision
  requires premise and evidence
  warns pending

domain ADR0029:
  description "ADR-0029 revision 2: Preserve the rejected revision-1 V2 reader proposal and record its disposition. Status Rejected."

problem P1:
  |
    Eight production character generations that were activated as ready V2 now
    fail read-time eligibility because a nonempty action-selector invariant was
    added without changing schemaVersion 2 or compiler version 2. Their stored
    rows remain ready, but match selection returns only the later Takumi generation.

premise AUTHORITY:
  |
    ADR-0010 owns immutable generations, explicit readiness and server-side
    eligibility. ADR-0027 owns one conscious judgment for goal, action and
    utterance, separate from non-deliberative psyche and engine validation.
    Requirement candidate revision 1 is at lifecycle step 2 and is not accepted.

premise TERMINOLOGY:
  |
    An executable action norm has a structured selector and may rank or constrain
    actions. A selectorless soft legacy statement can only provide awareness-gated
    conscious guidance. It is not an engine constraint and is not psyche state.

premise OPTIONS:
  |
    A: keep all selectorless V2 generations unsupported and require owner-triggered
    regeneration. This preserves current strictness but changes already-ready V2
    meaning and hides eight usable characters. B: restore the recorded compiler-v2
    soft-guidance interpretation only for an exact already-ready generation while
    requiring selectors for every new activation. C: rewrite old immutable
    generations or infer selectors. C violates immutability and invents behavior.

evidence E_PRODUCTION:
  |
    Read-only production inspection on 2026-09-10 found nine exact current
    generations persisted as ready. Current code evaluated Takumi ready and the
    other eight unsupported with invalid_action_norm_selector. Those eight contain
    twenty-one selectorless prefer norms, all force preference or commitment and
    no constraint. Sixteen additional owner characters have no ready V2 state.

evidence E_PATH:
  |
    MatchPage requests /api/characters?selectable=true. The route filters the DTO
    selectable flag. getCharacterCompatibility recomputes readiness with the new
    selector invariant, and battle binding uses the same strict ready assertion.

evidence E_HISTORY:
  |
    The selector requirement and compiler rejection were added under the existing
    V2 identifiers. Earlier compiler-v2 evaluation let selectorless soft statements
    contribute consciousStatement while they matched no action and therefore did
    not change mechanical ranking or exclusions. Current deterministic conversion
    no longer creates such entries; it defers unstructured principles to authoring.

evidence E_RCA:
  |
    docs/character-authoring-selection-rca-2026-09-10.llmthink.dsl identifies the
    read-time version reinterpretation and terminology debt. Its CLI audit reports
    fatal 0, error 0 and warning 0. It is reasoning evidence, not owner acceptance.

premise HISTORICAL_OWNER_ACCEPTANCE:
  |
    The product owner did not accept requirement candidate revision 1 or ADR-0029
    revision 1. The later accepted requirement revision 6 rejects a permanent V2
    compatibility reader and the owner accepted the recommended successor plan
    that records ADR-0029 as Rejected and creates a new numbered ADR.

decision D1 based_on P1, AUTHORITY, TERMINOLOGY, OPTIONS, E_PRODUCTION, E_HISTORY:
  |
    Propose option B. An exact current generation already marked ready may retain
    compiler-v2 compatibility when every selectorless entry is a soft prefer norm
    with preference or commitment force. Its statement remains awareness-gated
    conscious guidance. It never ranks, excludes, forces or fabricates an action.

decision D2 based_on D1, E_PATH, AUTHORITY:
  |
    Split persisted V2 compatibility validation from new-activation readiness.
    Persisted validation checks the V2 envelope, required compiler receipts, claim
    receipt and internal references, while allowing D1. New activation continues
    to reject every selectorless action norm. A read never changes readiness state,
    appends a generation or moves a pointer.

decision D3 based_on D1, D2, TERMINOLOGY:
  |
    Compiler-v2 accepts D1 entries only as conscious-only guidance. Selectorless
    constraints remain invalid. Tests prove that changing only the legacy statement
    can change the conscious-principle text but cannot change ranked or excluded
    action keys. Code and diagnostics use the legacy conscious-only qualifier.

decision D4 based_on D2, AUTHORITY, E_PRODUCTION:
  |
    Unsupported legacy or no-state rows remain unsupported, so this restores at
    most the eight observed exact ready V2 generations and does not make all owner
    characters selectable. No stored bytes are rewritten. A future dedicated
    conscious-principle field and explicit generation migration require another
    accepted decision.

decision D5 based_on D1, D2, D3, D4, E_RCA, HISTORICAL_OWNER_ACCEPTANCE:
  |
    Reject the revision-1 implementation direction. Preserve D1-D4 as historical
    proposal content, but do not use it as implementation authority. ADR-0030 is
    the Proposed successor direction. No V2 reader exception is implemented.
